Use a `FormInput` model with typed fields and a regex `pattern` on the receipt ID. Collect it with `wait_for_input`:

```python
from datetime import date

import mistralai.workflows as workflows
import mistralai.workflows.plugins.mistralai as workflows_mistralai
from mistralai.workflows.conversational import (
    FormInput,
    TextField,
    NumberField,
    DateField,
)


class ExpenseForm(FormInput):
    description: str = TextField(description="Expense description")
    amount: float = NumberField(
        description="Amount in USD",
        minimum=0,
        maximum=10_000,
    )
    expense_date: date = DateField(description="Date of expense")
    receipt_id: str = TextField(
        description="Receipt ID",
        pattern=r"^RCP-\d{6}$",  # e.g. RCP-123456
    )


@workflows.workflow.define(
    name="expense-submission-workflow",
    workflow_display_name="Expense Submission",
    workflow_description="Submit and validate an expense",
)
class ExpenseSubmissionWorkflow(workflows.InteractiveWorkflow):
    @workflows.workflow.entrypoint
    async def run(self) -> workflows_mistralai.ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput:
        expense = await self.wait_for_input(
            ExpenseForm,
            label="Submit Expense",
        )

        if not validate_expense(expense):
            return workflows_mistralai.ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput(
                content=[
                    workflows_mistralai.TextOutput(
                        text=f"Expense with receipt {expense.receipt_id} failed validation."
                    )
                ],
                isError=True,
            )

        return workflows_mistralai.ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput(
            content=[
                workflows_mistralai.TextOutput(
                    text=f"Expense {expense.receipt_id} was submitted successfully."
                )
            ]
        )
```

`TextField(pattern=...)` applies regex validation; the form’s other typed fields can use `NumberField`, `DateField`, and similar field types. [`Forms and confirmations`](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/interacting-with-workflows/conversational_workflows/forms_and_confirmations)

For a failed business validation, return `ChatAssistantWorkflowOutput` with `isError=True`. The `TextOutput` text becomes the error shown in the conversation, and Work marks the workflow as failed. [`Publish in Vibe — Error handling`](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/workflows/interacting-with-workflows/conversational_workflows/publish_in_vibe)
